IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `je21-nouns`
IMPORT `je21-seat-1-making-and-commencement`

-- je21-tests-seat-1-making-and-commencement: tests for the exported questions about what an instrument is, how it is made and when it starts.
-- The expected values were written by hand from Articles 1 to 3, 26 and the endnotes before the module was run.
-- The questions use the default reading of each fork, which je21-seat-defaults names; the other readings are tested in the rule modules' tests.

§ `Seat questions -- making and commencement -- tests`

§§ `Names for the instruments`

-- The seven facts: Regulations or Order or other instrument; made in Jersey; made under; adopted by the States; relies on other legislation; a UK Act provision; registered in the Royal Court.
`an instrument that is a Law` MEANS `Facts about an instrument` OF FALSE, TRUE, `neither of these`, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE
`Regulations made under a Law` MEANS `Facts about an instrument` OF TRUE, TRUE, `Jersey legislation`, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE
`an Order made under Regulations` MEANS `Facts about an instrument` OF TRUE, TRUE, `Jersey legislation`, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE
`a registered provision of a UK Act` MEANS `Facts about an instrument` OF FALSE, FALSE, `neither of these`, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE
`a provision of a UK Act not registered` MEANS `Facts about an instrument` OF FALSE, FALSE, `neither of these`, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE

§§ `The Law itself`

#ASSERT `Which text of the Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021 governs on a given day?` (YMD 2021 9 27) EQUALS `the Law was not in force`
#ASSERT `Which text of the Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021 governs on a given day?` (YMD 2021 9 28) EQUALS `the text of 28 September 2021`
#ASSERT `Which text of the Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021 governs on a given day?` (YMD 2024 1 10) EQUALS `the text of 28 September 2021`
#ASSERT `Which text of the Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021 governs on a given day?` (YMD 2024 1 11) EQUALS `the text of 11 January 2024`
#ASSERT NOT `Was the Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021 in force at some time on a given day?` (YMD 2021 9 27)
#ASSERT `Was the Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021 in force at some time on a given day?` (YMD 2021 9 28)

§§ `What an instrument is`

#ASSERT `Is this instrument Jersey legislation?` `an instrument that is a Law`
#ASSERT `Is this instrument Jersey legislation?` `Regulations made under a Law`
#ASSERT `Is this instrument Jersey legislation?` `an Order made under Regulations`
#ASSERT NOT `Is this instrument Jersey legislation?` `a registered provision of a UK Act`
#ASSERT NOT `Is this instrument Jersey legislation?` `a provision of a UK Act not registered`
#ASSERT `Is this instrument a Law?` `an instrument that is a Law`
#ASSERT NOT `Is this instrument a Law?` `Regulations made under a Law`
#ASSERT NOT `Is this instrument a Law?` `an Order made under Regulations`
#ASSERT NOT `Is this instrument a Law?` `a registered provision of a UK Act`
#ASSERT `Is this instrument Jersey subordinate legislation?` `Regulations made under a Law`
#ASSERT `Is this instrument Jersey subordinate legislation?` `an Order made under Regulations`
#ASSERT NOT `Is this instrument Jersey subordinate legislation?` `an instrument that is a Law`
#ASSERT NOT `Is this instrument Jersey subordinate legislation?` `a registered provision of a UK Act`
#ASSERT `Is this instrument UK extended legislation?` `a registered provision of a UK Act`
#ASSERT NOT `Is this instrument UK extended legislation?` `a provision of a UK Act not registered`
#ASSERT NOT `Is this instrument UK extended legislation?` `an instrument that is a Law`
#ASSERT NOT `Is this instrument UK extended legislation?` `Regulations made under a Law`

§§ `How a Law is made`

-- The steps: adopted on; sanctioned on; registered on; a taxation draft declared by Act.
`all three steps` MEANS `Steps toward making a Law` OF JUST (YMD 2022 2 1), JUST (YMD 2022 3 1), JUST (YMD 2022 3 15), FALSE
`adopted and sanctioned only` MEANS `Steps toward making a Law` OF JUST (YMD 2022 2 1), JUST (YMD 2022 3 1), NOTHING, FALSE
`adopted only` MEANS `Steps toward making a Law` OF JUST (YMD 2022 2 1), NOTHING, NOTHING, FALSE
`a taxation draft adopted and declared` MEANS `Steps toward making a Law` OF JUST (YMD 2022 2 1), NOTHING, NOTHING, TRUE
`no step taken` MEANS `Steps toward making a Law` OF NOTHING, NOTHING, NOTHING, FALSE

#ASSERT `Has this Law been made?` (YMD 2022 6 1) `all three steps` EQUALS RIGHT TRUE
#ASSERT `Has this Law been made?` (YMD 2022 6 1) `adopted and sanctioned only` EQUALS RIGHT FALSE
#ASSERT `Has this Law been made?` (YMD 2022 6 1) `adopted only` EQUALS RIGHT FALSE
#ASSERT `Has this Law been made?` (YMD 2022 6 1) `no step taken` EQUALS RIGHT FALSE
#ASSERT `Has this Law been made?` (YMD 2022 6 1) `a taxation draft adopted and declared` EQUALS RIGHT TRUE
-- Both texts of the Law give the same answer; only the words of Article 2(1)(b) differ.
#ASSERT `Has this Law been made?` (YMD 2023 12 31) `all three steps` EQUALS RIGHT TRUE
#ASSERT `Has this Law been made?` (YMD 2024 1 11) `all three steps` EQUALS RIGHT TRUE
-- Before the Law was in force: a value, not a refusal.
#ASSERT `Has this Law been made?` (YMD 2021 9 27) `all three steps` EQUALS LEFT (`the Law was not in force on that date` "28 September 2021 (R&O.112/2021), the day specified by Act of the States under Article 26")
#ASSERT `Has this Law been made?` (YMD 2021 9 28) `all three steps` EQUALS RIGHT TRUE

#ASSERT `On what day was this Law made?` (YMD 2022 6 1) `all three steps` EQUALS RIGHT (JUST (YMD 2022 3 15))
#ASSERT `On what day was this Law made?` (YMD 2022 6 1) `adopted and sanctioned only` EQUALS RIGHT NOTHING
#ASSERT `On what day was this Law made?` (YMD 2022 6 1) `no step taken` EQUALS RIGHT NOTHING
#ASSERT REFUSED `On what day was this Law made?` (YMD 2022 6 1) `a taxation draft adopted and declared` BECAUSE "Article 2(2) treats a taxation draft as made without the steps of Article 2(1)(b) and (c) and does not say on what day it was made"
#ASSERT `On what day was this Law made?` (YMD 2021 9 27) `all three steps` EQUALS LEFT (`the Law was not in force on that date` "28 September 2021 (R&O.112/2021), the day specified by Act of the States under Article 26")

§§ `How subordinate legislation is made`

-- The steps: its form; the proposition adopted on; signed on; signed by the person responsible; made by a body; signed per the body's procedure.
`Regulations adopted` MEANS `Steps toward making subordinate legislation` OF Regulations, JUST (YMD 2022 5 10), NOTHING, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`Regulations not adopted` MEANS `Steps toward making subordinate legislation` OF Regulations, NOTHING, NOTHING, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`an Order signed by the person responsible` MEANS `Steps toward making subordinate legislation` OF `an Order`, NOTHING, JUST (YMD 2022 6 1), TRUE, FALSE, FALSE
`an Order of a body signed in accordance with its procedure` MEANS `Steps toward making subordinate legislation` OF `an Order`, NOTHING, JUST (YMD 2022 6 2), FALSE, TRUE, TRUE
`an Order of a body signed otherwise` MEANS `Steps toward making subordinate legislation` OF `an Order`, NOTHING, JUST (YMD 2022 6 2), FALSE, TRUE, FALSE
`an Order not yet signed` MEANS `Steps toward making subordinate legislation` OF `an Order`, NOTHING, NOTHING, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE

#ASSERT `Has this subordinate legislation been made?` (YMD 2022 6 1) `Regulations adopted` EQUALS RIGHT TRUE
#ASSERT `Has this subordinate legislation been made?` (YMD 2022 6 1) `Regulations not adopted` EQUALS RIGHT FALSE
#ASSERT `Has this subordinate legislation been made?` (YMD 2022 6 1) `an Order signed by the person responsible` EQUALS RIGHT TRUE
#ASSERT `Has this subordinate legislation been made?` (YMD 2022 6 1) `an Order of a body signed in accordance with its procedure` EQUALS RIGHT TRUE
#ASSERT `Has this subordinate legislation been made?` (YMD 2022 6 1) `an Order of a body signed otherwise` EQUALS RIGHT FALSE
#ASSERT `Has this subordinate legislation been made?` (YMD 2022 6 1) `an Order not yet signed` EQUALS RIGHT FALSE
#ASSERT `Has this subordinate legislation been made?` (YMD 2021 9 27) `Regulations adopted` EQUALS LEFT (`the Law was not in force on that date` "28 September 2021 (R&O.112/2021), the day specified by Act of the States under Article 26")
#ASSERT `On what day was this subordinate legislation made?` (YMD 2022 6 1) `Regulations adopted` EQUALS RIGHT (JUST (YMD 2022 5 10))
#ASSERT `On what day was this subordinate legislation made?` (YMD 2022 6 1) `an Order signed by the person responsible` EQUALS RIGHT (JUST (YMD 2022 6 1))
#ASSERT `On what day was this subordinate legislation made?` (YMD 2022 6 1) `an Order of a body signed in accordance with its procedure` EQUALS RIGHT (JUST (YMD 2022 6 2))
#ASSERT `On what day was this subordinate legislation made?` (YMD 2022 6 1) `an Order of a body signed otherwise` EQUALS RIGHT NOTHING
#ASSERT `On what day was this subordinate legislation made?` (YMD 2022 6 1) `Regulations not adopted` EQUALS RIGHT NOTHING

§§ `When a provision that says nothing about it starts`

-- Legislation that only commences other legislation, and an Act referred to in Article 2(2): when made.
#ASSERT `On what day does a provision that says nothing about when it starts come into force?` `legislation having effect only to commence other legislation` (YMD 2022 3 1) EQUALS RIGHT (YMD 2022 3 1)
#ASSERT `On what day does a provision that says nothing about when it starts come into force?` `an Act of the States referred to in Article 2(2)` (YMD 2022 3 1) EQUALS RIGHT (YMD 2022 3 1)
-- Any other legislation: the day after it is made, across a month end, a leap day, a year end.
#ASSERT `On what day does a provision that says nothing about when it starts come into force?` `any other legislation` (YMD 2022 3 1) EQUALS RIGHT (YMD 2022 3 2)
#ASSERT `On what day does a provision that says nothing about when it starts come into force?` `any other legislation` (YMD 2022 2 28) EQUALS RIGHT (YMD 2022 3 1)
#ASSERT `On what day does a provision that says nothing about when it starts come into force?` `any other legislation` (YMD 2024 2 28) EQUALS RIGHT (YMD 2024 2 29)
#ASSERT `On what day does a provision that says nothing about when it starts come into force?` `any other legislation` (YMD 2024 2 29) EQUALS RIGHT (YMD 2024 3 1)
#ASSERT `On what day does a provision that says nothing about when it starts come into force?` `any other legislation` (YMD 2022 12 31) EQUALS RIGHT (YMD 2023 1 1)
-- Made on the day the Law came into force, and the day before.
#ASSERT `On what day does a provision that says nothing about when it starts come into force?` `any other legislation` (YMD 2021 9 28) EQUALS RIGHT (YMD 2021 9 29)
#ASSERT `On what day does a provision that says nothing about when it starts come into force?` `any other legislation` (YMD 2021 9 27) EQUALS LEFT (`the Law was not in force on that date` "28 September 2021 (R&O.112/2021), the day specified by Act of the States under Article 26")

§§ `The time of day a provision that says nothing about it starts`

`ten past nine` MEANS `Time of day` OF 9, 10
`noon` MEANS `Time of day` OF 12, 0
`no time known` MEANS NOTHING
`made at ten past nine` MEANS JUST (`Time of day` OF 9, 10)

-- Any other legislation made on 1 March 2022: not in force on the day it is made; on the day after the Law does not say; later days, yes.
#ASSERT NOT `Was a provision that says nothing about when it starts in force at a given time of day?` `any other legislation` (YMD 2022 3 1) `no time known` (YMD 2022 3 1) `noon`
#ASSERT REFUSED `Was a provision that says nothing about when it starts in force at a given time of day?` `any other legislation` (YMD 2022 3 1) `no time known` (YMD 2022 3 2) `noon` BECAUSE "the Law does not say at what time of the day after it is made a provision that is silent as to its commencement comes into force"
#ASSERT `Was a provision that says nothing about when it starts in force at a given time of day?` `any other legislation` (YMD 2022 3 1) `no time known` (YMD 2022 3 3) `noon`
-- Legislation that only commences other legislation starts when made: from the time of making if known.
#ASSERT `Was a provision that says nothing about when it starts in force at a given time of day?` `legislation having effect only to commence other legislation` (YMD 2022 3 1) `made at ten past nine` (YMD 2022 3 1) `noon`
#ASSERT `Was a provision that says nothing about when it starts in force at a given time of day?` `legislation having effect only to commence other legislation` (YMD 2022 3 1) `made at ten past nine` (YMD 2022 3 1) `ten past nine`
#ASSERT NOT `Was a provision that says nothing about when it starts in force at a given time of day?` `legislation having effect only to commence other legislation` (YMD 2022 3 1) `made at ten past nine` (YMD 2022 3 1) (`Time of day` OF 9, 9)
#ASSERT NOT `Was a provision that says nothing about when it starts in force at a given time of day?` `legislation having effect only to commence other legislation` (YMD 2022 3 1) `made at ten past nine` (YMD 2022 2 28) `noon`
#ASSERT REFUSED `Was a provision that says nothing about when it starts in force at a given time of day?` `legislation having effect only to commence other legislation` (YMD 2022 3 1) `no time known` (YMD 2022 3 1) `noon` BECAUSE "the time of day at which the legislation was made is not given, so whether it was in force at a time of day on the day it was made cannot be answered"

§§ `Legislation that started before Part 2 did`

#ASSERT `Does Article 3 govern when this legislation started?` NOTHING
#ASSERT NOT `Does Article 3 govern when this legislation started?` (JUST (YMD 2021 9 27))
#ASSERT `Does Article 3 govern when this legislation started?` (JUST (YMD 2021 9 28))
#ASSERT `Does Article 3 govern when this legislation started?` (JUST (YMD 2021 9 29))
#ASSERT NOT `Does Article 3 govern when this legislation started?` (JUST (YMD 1990 1 1))

§§ `Commencement by Ministerial Order, and different days for different provisions`

#ASSERT `Can these Regulations provide that they start by an Order of a Minister?` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT REFUSED `Can these Regulations provide that they start by an Order of a Minister?` TRUE TRUE BECAUSE "Article 3(3) lets Regulations provide this unless provision is made to the contrary, and the Law does not say whether any other instrument can, or what follows where provision is made to the contrary"
#ASSERT REFUSED `Can these Regulations provide that they start by an Order of a Minister?` FALSE FALSE BECAUSE "Article 3(3) lets Regulations provide this unless provision is made to the contrary, and the Law does not say whether any other instrument can, or what follows where provision is made to the contrary"
#ASSERT `Can a commencement power name different days, times or events for different provisions?` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT REFUSED `Can a commencement power name different days, times or events for different provisions?` TRUE FALSE BECAUSE "Article 3(4) speaks of a Law, Regulations made under a Law or a provision of either that may be commenced by Act or Order on a specified day, and the Law does not say whether any other power can name different days, times or events"
#ASSERT REFUSED `Can a commencement power name different days, times or events for different provisions?` FALSE TRUE BECAUSE "Article 3(4) speaks of a Law, Regulations made under a Law or a provision of either that may be commenced by Act or Order on a specified day, and the Law does not say whether any other power can name different days, times or events"

§§ `Amending legislation that has not come into force`

#ASSERT NOT `Does an amendment of uncommenced legislation commence it?` TRUE
#ASSERT REFUSED `Does an amendment of uncommenced legislation commence it?` FALSE BECAUSE "Article 3(5) deals only with an amendment of legislation or a provision that has not come into force"
-- The amendment starts when the provision amended starts, unless provision is made otherwise.
#ASSERT `On what day does an amendment of uncommenced legislation start?` (JUST (YMD 2023 4 1)) FALSE NOTHING EQUALS JUST (YMD 2023 4 1)
#ASSERT `On what day does an amendment of uncommenced legislation start?` NOTHING FALSE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `On what day does an amendment of uncommenced legislation start?` (JUST (YMD 2023 4 1)) TRUE (JUST (YMD 2023 5 1)) EQUALS JUST (YMD 2023 5 1)
#ASSERT REFUSED `On what day does an amendment of uncommenced legislation start?` (JUST (YMD 2023 4 1)) TRUE NOTHING BECAUSE "provision is made otherwise, and the moment it gives is not supplied"
